# Build-time configuration for the frontend.
#
# Copy to `.env.production` — NOT `.env.local`. Vite loads `.env.local` in every
# mode including `vite dev`, which would silently point your local dev server at
# the deployed API and make the local invite code stop working. `.env.production`
# is only read by `vite build`, which is exactly what deployment needs.
#
# In development, leave all of these unset: the dev server proxies /api to
# `wrangler dev`, so everything is same-origin with no CORS.

# Base URL of the deployed Worker API.
VITE_API_URL=https://futsal-friday-api.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev

# Public URL of this app, used in the "copy summary" text so people who see the
# message in the group chat can find their way in.
VITE_APP_URL=https://futsal-friday.pages.dev

# There is deliberately no VAPID key here: the frontend fetches the application
# server key from GET /push/status, so it can never drift from the private key
# the Worker signs with after a rotation.
